---
type Props = { city?: string };
const { city } = Astro.props;
const where = city ? ` in ${city}` : "";
---

<h2>Three kinds of water{where}</h2>
<p>
  Restoration people sort water by how dirty it is. That changes whether you
  should stay in the room and what a crew will throw out.
</p>
<div class="split">
  <div class="card">
    <h3>Clean water</h3>
    <p>
      A supply line, ice maker, or water heater that has not sat. You can often
      stay in the house. Fast drying still matters so it does not turn into a
      dirty job.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
    <h3>Gray water</h3>
    <p>
      Washing machine, dishwasher, fridge drip pan, or a toilet bowl overflow
      without feces. Treat it as unclean. Gloves. Do not use a household vac
      you will use later on dry carpet.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>
<div class="card" style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
  <h3>Sewage and flood from outside</h3>
  <p>
    Toilet backup with waste, sewer line, river or street flood. Stay out of
    it. Kids and pets out. This is not a towel job.     Tell the form it is sewage
    so the shop sends the right crew.
  </p>
</div>
